From: jempa <jempamartensson@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:54:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/47] VolPath: MIS per infinite light for escaping rays (for
 hdPbrt)

The escaped-ray loop multiplied r_l by each infinite light's pdf in place,
so a second infinite light with radiance in the same direction got the
product of both pdfs: its BSDF-sampled contribution was weighted almost 1
on top of light sampling (fireflies with a dome and a distant light's cone,
pbrt patch 10, depending on their order).
---
 src/pbrt/cpu/integrators.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pbrt/cpu/integrators.cpp b/src/pbrt/cpu/integrators.cpp
index b758ce4..c6d68c0 100644
--- a/src/pbrt/cpu/integrators.cpp
+++ b/src/pbrt/cpu/integrators.cpp
@@ -1219,10 +1219,12 @@ SampledSpectrum VolPathIntegrator::Li(RayDifferential ray, SampledWavelengths &l
                         L += beta * Le / HdPbrtMisAverage(r_u, lambda);
                     else {
                         // Add infinite light contribution using both PDFs with MIS
+                        // hdPbrt: per light (pbrt multiplied r_l in place, so a
+                        // second infinite light lit in the same direction, e.g. a
+                        // dome and a distant light's cone, got both lights' pdfs).
                         Float p_l = lightSampler.PMF(prevIntrContext, light) *
                                     light.PDF_Li(prevIntrContext, ray.d, true);
-                        r_l *= p_l;
-                        L += beta * Le / HdPbrtMisAverage((r_u + r_l), lambda);
+                        L += beta * Le / HdPbrtMisAverage((r_u + r_l * p_l), lambda);
                     }
                 }
             }
